# Image check (no conversion)

This applies to **every image on the site**: project covers, writing heroes, in-article photos, UI screenshots, illustrations. Not only new uploads.

When the user provides an image, **inspect only**. Do not convert, resize, recompress, or transcode.

1. Read width, height, and format
2. Compare against the spec below
3. If it fails, stop. Tell them exactly what to change (format, width, height, destination). Wait for a new file
4. If it passes, copy the file as-is and point MDX/frontmatter at that path

Do not use chat attachments as a source to “fix” — Cursor often saves them at 1024px. Report that and ask for the correct export.

## Spec

| Use | Path | Format | Size |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Project cover / hero (same 16:9 as the home card) | `public/projects/<slug>/` | `.webp` | **1920×1080** |
| Writing `#wide` (full column breakout) | `public/writing/<slug>/` | `.webp` | **1600–1920px** |
| Photo in the text column | `public/writing/<slug>/` | `.webp` | max **1600px** |
| UI screenshot | `public/writing/<slug>/` or `public/projects/<slug>/` | `.webp` | max **1920px** |
| Flat illustration, logo, art with type | same folders | WebP lossless or SVG | do not enlarge |

- Do not enlarge smaller assets
- Reject native captures (e.g. 3024px Retina PNGs) and PNG/JPEG photos/screenshots
- Point MDX frontmatter `image` and markdown `![]()` at the `.webp` path

```mdx
image: '/writing/my-slug/hero.webp'
![Alt text](/writing/my-slug/hero.webp#wide "Caption")
```

## Rendering

- Article images go through `ZoomableImage` + `next/image` with real `width`/`height` from `getPublicImageSize`
- Do not use a raw `<img>` for post content
- Keep `next.config.mjs` `images.formats` as AVIF then WebP

## Leave as PNG/SVG

PWA and platform icons only: `app/icon.svg`, `app/favicon.ico`, `app/apple-icon.png`, `public/icon-192.png`, `public/icon-512.png`
